{%- comment -%}
  The advertorial harness's page template (cycle 84, 2026-10-07).
  Source of truth: the harness repo, deploy/shopify/templates/page.pk-harness.liquid.
  Push it with deploy/shopify/push_template.py; do not edit it in the theme editor.

  The harness sets template_suffix "pk-harness" on every page it publishes
  (tenant.yaml shopify_publish.template_suffix).
  Its body_html carries all of its own CSS in one body <style> block, so this
  template prints page.content raw: no section, no .rte wrapper, no container,
  no theme page title. It uses no section or snippet, so it renders the same in
  every theme that holds it. The theme layout still loads (head, fonts,
  analytics, app scripts).

  Hidden theme chrome (header, announcement bar, footer): the same selectors
  as templates/page.pk-regret-lp.liquid. The page body never holds a bare
  <header> or <footer> (harness/page_body.py strip_document_chrome turns a
  classed one into a <div>), so the element selectors cannot hide page content.
  Rollback: docs/PUBLISHING.md "Storefront template (cycle 84)".
{%- endcomment -%}
<style id="pk-harness-hide-chrome">
  header, #shopify-section-header, .header-wrapper, [data-site-header], .shopify-section-group-header-group, [class*="shopify-section-group-main-header"], #shopify-section-static-header { display: none !important }
  footer:not(cart-drawer footer), #shopify-section-footer, [id^="shopify-section-footer"], .shopify-section-group-footer-group, [class*="shopify-section-group-main-footer"] { display: none !important }
  #shopify-section-announcement-bar, .announcement-bar, #shopify-section-announcement, .announcement_bar, .promo-bar:not(body) { display: none !important }
  #MainContent, .main-content { padding-top: 0 !important; margin-top: 0 !important; padding-bottom: 0 !important; margin-bottom: 0 !important }
</style>
{{ page.content }}
